WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:04.300
Just what tricks do "The Batman" director
Matt Reeves and his crew have up their sleeves

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.300
for audiences?

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.130
Could the riddle be…on us?

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:10.400
Keep watching for one big twist the movie
has in store.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.030
Batman has his hands full in the newest entry
to the Dark Knight movie mythos.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:17.529
This time around, The Riddler is a serial
killer targeting Gotham's elite to bring their

00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:19.099
corruption to light.

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:22.580
Catwoman seems like she may be an ally, but
as tends to be the case throughout her history

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.650
with the Bat, she causes her own share of
headaches.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.750
And The Penguin rubs elbows with the most
dangerous criminals in all of Gotham through

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.929
his nightclub.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:33.949
Batman's arguably the busiest person in Gotham,
and that's just the beginning of his problems.

00:00:33.949 --> 00:00:37.969
However, people with fun nicknames who sometimes
wear costumes are only part of the equation.

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:42.449
There are plenty of criminals who keep a lower
profile, and that's where Carmine Falcone

00:00:42.449 --> 00:00:43.930
enters the picture.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.550
He's a crime lord who's awfully chummy with
Penguin and has a history of keeping the most

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.929
powerful people in the city under his thumb.

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:54.219
He's a menacing force that lurks in the shadows,
and while he may not be as flashy, he's just

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:56.300
as, if not more, terrifying.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.929
Given his proclivity for criminal activity,
it makes one of the movie's primary twists

00:00:59.929 --> 00:01:01.430
all the more shocking.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:05.260
In "The Batman," Riddler sets out to reveal
a massive conspiracy in which Gotham's elite

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:08.540
power brokers took funds from the Wayne Foundation's
Renewal project.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:13.250
That project had dedicated $1 billion per
year to help Gothamites, but the conspiracists

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.110
lined their own pockets instead.

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:18.550
But there's a rat in their midst, and The
Riddler wants this individual to come to light

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.370
to pay for their actions.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:23.570
Batman and Police Lieutenant James Gordon
attempt to find this rat, knowing he'll be

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.210
the next Riddler victim.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.160
They have several guesses initially with the
only clue being the Spanish phrase, "rata

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.810
alada," which roughly translates to "winged
rat."

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.890
At first, Batman assumes the rat must be the
Penguin, since penguins have wings.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:40.240
When that turns out to be a dead end, he wonders
if he's at the center of this conspiracy somehow

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.630
since bats are sometimes derogatorily called
rats with wings.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.730
But that's when he has the realization that
"Falcone" has "falcon" right there in the

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:48.730
name.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:49.830
And falcons have wings!

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:54.540
"It all adds up to a sinister riddle.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.540
Riddl-er.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.910
Riddler?"]

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:01.390
It's a development that likely took plenty
of fans by surprise.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:05.660
In the comics, Falcone is a ruthless mob boss
known as "The Roman" in honor of his ruthless

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.660
demeanor.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.500
He keeps more to the shadows in "The Batman,"
and his turn as the rat is a significant departure

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.890
from his depictions in comics, TV shows, and
other movies.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.530
No doubt it took plenty of audience members
by surprise, just one of the many shocking

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.730
moments to be found in "The Batman."

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:23.380
Carmine Falcone doesn't get a ton of screentime
in "The Batman," but he makes excellent use

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.020
of the scenes he does appear in.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.110
It goes along perfectly with his attitude.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:31.319
He can be a more effective crime lord if he
keeps a low profile and stays out of the public

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:32.750
eye as often as possible.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.270
However, it's clear he gets into ample trouble
behind the scenes.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:40.350
As it turns out, he's not just a rat, but
also the father of a Cat.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.200
He's Selina Kyle, a.k.a.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.380
Catowoman's dad.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.500
Granted, some fans were probably more likely
to see this particular twist coming, seeing

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.920
how there's precedent for it in the comic
books.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.410
Their relationship is hinted at in "The Long
Halloween" and its sequel.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:56.910
In the movie, Catwoman knows for sure that
Falcone is her father, but he's completely

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.580
unaware of her existence.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:02.440
He only learns the truth when she reveals
herself to him and mentions her mother, Maria

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.200
Kyle, to his face.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.260
Selina Kyle may be okay with letting Falcone
live in the comics, but she's out for blood

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.170
in "The Batman," missing her chance for revenge
when Batman enters the picture and stops her

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:14.530
before she does something she might regret.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.770
This isn't the first time Carmine Falcone
has appeared in a live-action film — he

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:21.959
was a key part of "Batman Begins" — but
Reeves and crew have created a terrifying

00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:25.319
mobster who's unlike any iteration in the
past.

